# SUPERSEDED by deploy/nginx.conf.
#
# This file served one shared app shell for an explicit allow-list of known
# routes — the right approach before prerendering existed, and its own
# comment said as much: "This duplication disappears the moment the site
# moves to pre-rendered per-route HTML." That's what deploy/nginx.conf now
# does (scripts/prerender.js generates a real static file per route per
# locale), carrying forward everything still relevant from this file: the
# HTTPS/www canonicalization, security headers, and crawler-file handling.
#
# I couldn't delete this file directly (a sandbox limitation on my end) —
# safe to delete by hand: `git rm deploy/nginx.conf.example`.
#
# See deploy/nginx.conf and DEPLOY.md.
